There are different ways to terminate a C program:

1. Using the return statement:

If your program is a function, you can use the return statement to terminate the function and return a value to the calling function. The program will terminate when the main function returns.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int add(int a, int b) {
    int sum = a + b;
    return sum;
}

int main() {
    int x = 10, y = 20;
    int result = add(x, y);
    printf("The sum is: %d\n", result);
    return 0;
}
```

2. Using the exit() function:

The exit() function is a standard library function that is declared in the stdlib.h file. It is used to terminate the program immediately with a status code that you specify.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    // Your program code here
    // ...
    // If you want to

